Cambridge B2 First Listening Part 2 for an English-speaking learner: one speaker talking for 3 to 4 minutes about their work, a hobby or an experience, with sentence completion: each question is a sentence with a gap, filled with a word or short phrase the speaker says. Gaps target concrete details with distractors nearby (two things mentioned, one corrected). Exactly 6 questions; accepted answers fit a short phrase and are listed once. Played twice. British English.